 ### Gradient Detachment in Training
-A training strategy where the object field component is detached from the backbone to prevent gradient backpropagation to the rendering part, ensuring independent optimization [S26, unofficial]. With detach, the object field component output is detached so gradients do not backpropagate to the NeRF backbone; without detach, gradients from the object field component backpropagate to the NeRF backbone, causing mutual influence [S26, unofficial]. The hyper-parameter $\Delta d$ for empty 3D point losses is tested at 0.025, 0.05, 0.10 meters, with 0.05 meters being optimal [S26, unofficial]. With detach achieves better scene rendering and decomposition quality, while without detach causes a significant drop in rendering quality [S26, unofficial].
